  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Increasing showers and thunderstorms today. \n\n-  Temperatures cooling through the weekend, running 10 degrees\n   below normal by Sunday.\n\n-  Brief warm up early next week, followed by another cool down.\n\nToday-Sunday:\n\nBeginning this morning, an upper-level low over Western Canada \nwill elongate southward and close off over Washington state. \nShowers and isolated thunderstorms will develop early today, \nbecoming more widespread through the afternoon as a cold front \nsweeps through the region. Frontal forcing may support a few \nstronger storms capable of erratic wind gusts, primarily along and\nsouth of Highway 12 in western Montana.\n\n* Wetting Rain: Probabilities reach 50% to 70% across west-\n  central Montana, southwest Montana, and Lemhi County. Confidence\n  decreases further north, where probabilities drop below 30% \n  across northwest Montana.\n\n* Sunday Outlook: High temperatures in the valleys will fall into\n  the upper 60s to low 70s roughly 10F below seasonal averages. \n  Although breezy winds will persist, higher relative humidity and\n  cooler temperatures will keep fire weather concerns low.\n\nMonday-Late Next Week:\n\nBrief high-pressure ridging rebounds Monday and Tuesday, bringing\na temporary return to temperatures in the 80s. This warm-up will \nbe short-lived, however, as ensemble guidance indicates another \nunseasonably cold and potentially wetter low-pressure system \narriving mid-to-late next week.",
